    'f.procs':'Leftover processes','sys.sweepNow':'Clean now','sys.sweeping':'cleaning…','sys.sweepDone':'closed {n}','sys.sweepBusy':'busy — will retry later','f.doc.procs':'## Definition\nBrowser processes zemory started that nobody uses any more — web-scan windows or probe runs left behind when their parent died.\n## Why this row exists\nProcess junk is not in git status and takes no visible space; you only notice it when Task Manager fills with strange processes. Measured 2026-09-12: 75 headless Edge processes alive since the morning, each holding a temp profile.\n## How it works\n• The background sweep runs every 6 hours (same tick that cleans scratch dirs and old profiles).\n• This row only COUNTS; the Clean now button is what actually closes them.\n## Four safety stops\n• only zemory\'s own profiles (a slot, or a zemory-* temp dir) — your normal browser is never touched;\n• HEADLESS only: a window you can see is a login window waiting for you, never auto-closed;\n• must be older than 30 minutes to count as orphaned;\n• if a web scan is running, nothing is touched.','sys.health':'Health {ok}/{n} OK','sys.hint':'Click a feature on the left → description + Check / Toggle on the right','sys.recheckAll':'Recheck all','sys.rechecking':'checking…','sys.rechecked':'done','sys.pick':'Select a feature on the left.','sys.on':'On','sys.off':'Off','sys.buildMissing':'Build missing digests','sys.buildNow':'Build digest now','sys.recheck':'Recheck','sys.goto':'Go to',
